WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.234
-We're back with
Jennifer Hudson.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.070
You know, every time
you've been on the show,

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.538
we have talked about
your accomplishments,

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.206
but you had a really big one
since last time you're here.

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:08.774
You were a producer
on a Broadway show.

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:10.342
-Yes.
-"A Strange Loop."

00:00:10.342 --> 00:00:12.412
-"A Strange Loop."
-Won a Tony.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.714
That was your Tony
that completed an EGOT.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:20.119
You've got all four --
Emmy, Grammy, Oscar, Tony.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:21.721
-Yeah, that was surreal.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.723
You know, I went
in support of the cast.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.024
-Yeah.
-And when they said

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:27.560
"Strange Loop" won
for Best Musical,

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.795
I'm up there cheering
for the cast,

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:32.532
and everyone started chanting,
"EGOT, EGOT."

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:35.535
and I'm like, oh, whoa.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.270
I just won an EGOT.
-Yeah.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.804
-Yeah.
-They say that EGOT's

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:40.807
most likely to happen when you
don't know it's happened.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.075
-[ Laughs ] I guess so.

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:46.913
-It's like a watched tea kettle
never whatever --

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.815
You know what I mean?
They say that about EGOTs.

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:54.820
So did you -- now you've got --
How do you display them?

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.057
-Well, I have an award wall
in my home in Chicago,

00:00:58.057 --> 00:00:59.358
and the Oscar
sits in the middle.

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:01.026
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:01:01.026 --> 00:01:03.029
And it says, "Haaaa!"

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.832
And I said I would never
reveal the award wall

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.200
until the EGOT was complete.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.535
But now that it is,
I think I need to,

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:14.040
like, redo the award wall,
and then I'll reveal it.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.943
-I think you should have, like,
a mechanical sliding wall.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.378
And when people come in,
they just see the Emmy,

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:20.713
and you're like,
yeah, I just won an Emmy.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.416
And then you hit a button
and it's like,

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:26.085
oh, that's right,
I also have a Grammy.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:28.787
Well, I'm sure
that's all of it.

00:01:28.787 --> 00:01:31.024
[ Both imitating door opening ]

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.458
-I like that.
-Yeah. That's fun, right?

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.928
-You gon' wake up
and I'm gon' have it now, okay?

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.829
-I have good ideas about it

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:39.331
because I'm never going to
win the awards.

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:41.868
So you know what? I will give it
to you as a gift. Yeah.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.971
-Okay. All right.
I will hold on to that.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:48.307
-Do you have any dream guests?
Throw it out in the universe

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:49.575
for the next time you're here.

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:50.776
Who would you like to have on?

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:55.014
-Of course, Taylor Swift.
I would love to have her.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:58.017
Um, Michael Jordan
is a dream of mine.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:01.153
I know, I know
that's a tough dream.

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:03.956
And if I could pick Zendaya.
-Oh, that's a good three.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:06.158
-Yeah, yeah.
-That's a good three.

00:02:06.158 --> 00:02:08.761
Well, I wish that
you get all of that.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.896
I feel like
with everything you have,

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:12.865
I can't imagine you're not
going to get that as well.

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:14.566
-Okay.
-And now you were talking

00:02:14.566 --> 00:02:16.402
about your son, and how many --

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.771
how often does
he come and see your show?

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.374
-Not often, because
he's a basketball kid.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.342
So he's heavily into sports.

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:24.711
-Okay.
How old is he now?

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.078
-He's 14.
-Oh, yeah. There you go.

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:28.647
-Yes. And now he's going
to school out in LA.

00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:30.149
-Okay.
-So that's a new thing.

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:32.451
Before, I could drop him off at
school and then go to work.

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:34.254
-That's very exciting.
-Yes, it's very exciting.

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:36.289
-So you do need to have like
a basketball guest on the show

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.590
to have him show
any interest at all?

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.225
-I mean, then I'll be cool.
-Yeah?

00:02:40.225 --> 00:02:42.762
It breaks my heart that
you're not cool to your son.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:45.231
-You know? To your kids,
you're just Mom.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.699
-Yeah. That's true.
-Yeah.

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.267
-No matter how many people --
like,

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.835
when I walk my kids to school,
every now and then,

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:50.970
people will be like,
"Hey, I love your show."

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.238
And they're like,
"Oh, what's that about?"

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.006
I'm like, "I have a show."
They're like, "When?"

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:55.374
-See?
-Yeah.

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:57.843
-Exactly. So you understand.
-Yeah. It's heartbreaking.

00:02:57.843 --> 00:02:59.378
You know what my son said to me
the other day?

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:03.849
"When you die,
do I get your show?"

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:08.087
-David, don't you say that
to me. [ Laughs ]

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.755
Mine told me,
"Don't embarrass me."

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:11.457
-Oh, yeah. That's fair.

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:12.792
That's fair
not to be embarrassed.

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.594
Mine aren't old enough
to know what shame is yet.

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:16.329
-Well, you just wait.
-I know.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.729
You know what we do
every year?

00:03:17.729 --> 00:03:19.399
And we'll do it -- We're going
to film it this week.

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:22.301
So every Thanksgiving
since my son was --

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.236
I guess he was six months old

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:26.639
when we did our
Thanksgiving show.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.775
We dressed him up as a turkey --
like as a baby in a turkey suit.

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.110
And then we've been
adding each year,

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.046
and now I got three kids
that we're dressing up

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.514
in a turkey suit.
And one of these days,

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:36.449
one of his friends at school
is going to be like,

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.985
"I saw you dressed
like a [bleep] turkey."

00:03:39.985 --> 00:03:41.387
And he's going to come home
and be like,

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.489
"I did not consent to this."

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.857
-See?
-That day is going to come.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.225
-See?
-That day is gonna come.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:49.862
-Get ready.
-Yeah. Well, whatever.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.297
Look, he should be happy.
When I die,

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:53.699
all of this is his.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:55.201
-That is true.
-That is true.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:58.203
-That is true.
-Did you have any --

00:03:58.203 --> 00:03:59.872
you know, like, when
I got this show, you know,

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.141
I obviously had in mind
the people who had it before,

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.542
you know, from Letterman
to Conan to Jimmy.

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:04.811
Like, what were
the daytime shows

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:06.912
that you were most impressed by?

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:08.214
-Well, of course, Oprah,

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:11.117
I loved -- I grew up
watching Oprah's show.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:13.586
I love "The Ellen Show" as well.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:16.122
And then I'm into like,
Tamron and Sherri

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.423
now as well, too.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:18.724
-That's really cool.
It's really cool

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:20.993
to have those people
that were trailblazers that have

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.895
this path made for you.
It's really wonderful to watch.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.396
-Yeah, I get
to learn from them all.

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:26.565
-There you go.
-And have my host voice.

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:27.967
-Yeah, you're very good.

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.034
Thank you for
making it back here.

00:04:29.034 --> 00:04:30.570
And congratulations
on everything.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.671
-Thank you for having me.
-You guys,

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.572
that's Jennifer Hudson.

00:04:33.572 --> 00:04:35.874
"The Jennifer Hudson Show"
airs weekdays.

00:04:35.874 --> 00:04:36.909
Check your local listings

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.411
and stick around
for Matt Rogers.

